Job Description

Collaborate in building and perfecting mechanisms, policies, and internal regulations concerning IT security within the assigned scope:
- Collaborate in drafting, reviewing, and proposing amendments or replacements for VCBS's existing IT security mechanisms, policies, and internal regulations to meet practical operational requirements and comply with current legal provisions;
- Develop plans to evaluate and test the IT security of infrastructure systems and applications; analyze potential IT risks to propose and monitor the implementation of measures to ensure IT security for VCBS's IT systems;
- Collaborate in drafting, reviewing, and proposing modifications to procedures for responding to IT security incidents. Implement responses to security incidents as assigned;
- Develop training plans for IT security according to the company's internal regulations. Monitor compliance with IT security policies within the assigned scope:
- Ensure compliance with IT security policies and manage IT risk at VCBS;
- Coordinate with relevant departments to ensure that approved security requirements are met;
- Propose and support, supervise the implementation of corrective measures for IT security incidents.
Participate in professional training as per the department's plan; Fulfill other tasks assigned by the department leader.

Requirements
1. Education: Bachelor's degree or higher in Information Technology, Information Security, Electronics Telecommunications, Mathematics and Informatics, etc.; Language proficiency: Ability to read and understand English technical documents; Computer skills: Proficient in Word/Excel/Powerpoint functions.
2. Experience: At least 2 years of experience in Information Security/Cybersecurity; Direct project experience with ISMS or ISO 27001; Knowledge of IT security standards such as Cyber Security Framework (CSF), NIST, and legal regulations on information security; Preference for candidates holding relevant IT audit certifications or information security certifications.
3. Skills: Teamwork skills; Analytical, evaluative, and information synthesis thinking.

Salary and Benefits
- Competitive salary based on market rates and performance-based income;
- Meal allowances and other benefits;
- Full social insurance, health insurance, and other welfare benefits as per regulations;
- Health care insurance package and medical support for employees and their families;
- Numerous opportunities for promotion;
- Maximum conditions to fully utilize capabilities.
- Professional and civilized working environment.

Application
Candidates must submit an application form (mandatory) available at https://tuyendung.vcbs.com.vn/ under Career Opportunities, detailing work experience and training history. VCBS prefers early submissions; recruitment may end before the deadline if suitable candidates are found. VCBS will only contact qualified applicants for interviews. Contact: Ms. Han, Tel: 0243.936.6990 ext. 827.

