Job Description

1. Ensure strict adherence to the company's safety management system and client requirements:
   - Attend training sessions on quality policies and safety policies at the construction site;
   - Supervise and remind supervisors, construction teams, crane operators, transportation groups, subcontractors, and suppliers to adhere to safety regulations;
   - Closely monitor the assigned work area/site to control safety measures and identify potential safety hazards;
   - Analyze job safety and potential risks during construction to warn construction managers in charge of taking timely safety measures;
   - Participate in accident investigations and instruct workers to take corrective actions as required by the department head.

2. Organize training, information dissemination, and awareness campaigns on occupational health and safety:
   - Adhere to and promptly implement all procedures, policies, processes, rules, and regulations of the company and site management;
   - Propose innovative solutions to enhance work efficiency.

3. Daily site reporting or immediate reporting when issues arise:
   - Report daily on occupational health and safety matters to the department head and client;
   - Provide monthly and quarterly reports on occupational health and safety at assigned sites;
   - Make urgent reports or report incidents to direct or indirect superiors as needed.

Job Requirements
- Male, age between 23 and 45, good health, able to handle work pressure;
- College/University degree in Occupational Safety and Health, Engineering, Environmental Science;
- At least one year of relevant experience;
- In-depth knowledge of Occupational Health and Safety;
- Proficient in on-site safety supervision, professional English for communication;
- Hold a Group 2 Safety Certificate and Fire Prevention Training Certification;
- Strong communication skills, quick thinking, and effective problem-solving abilities;
- Proficient in MS Office;
- Able to work independently or in teams, manage time well, and handle tasks efficiently.

